Copied unchanged; every later change listed below with its test.

Built outside the bellwether workspace:
- crates/vendor/Cargo.toml is its workspace. It repeats the
  [workspace.package] and [workspace.dependencies] of Flockbook's
  xplat/Cargo.toml, which this manifest reads with `*.workspace = true`.
- crates/vendor/Cargo.lock started as Flockbook's xplat/Cargo.lock at
  the same commit; cargo kept only this crate's packages, at the same
  versions.
- The root workspace excludes crates/vendor because this code is not
  rustfmt-formatted and fails clippy -D warnings on Rust 1.99.1
  (redundant_guard, unnecessary_map_or, needless_lifetimes,
  collapsible_match, int_plus_one, type_complexity). Its tests run in
  scripts/test.sh.
- tests/common/mod.rs and tests/parser.rs read fixtures from
  ../../Tests/HerdrKitTests/Fixtures. The 14 files they use are copied
  unchanged from Flockbook's Tests/HerdrKitTests/Fixtures to
  crates/Tests/HerdrKitTests/Fixtures (the hub/ folder is not used).

Changes:
- 2026-11-06, src/resolver.rs: Codex sub-agent rollouts are skipped.
  `codex_meta_full` (new, with `CodexMeta`) reads the session id and
  whether `session_meta.payload.source` is an object with `subagent`;
  `codex_meta_data` calls it. `codex_candidates` and `codex_matches`
  leave sub-agents out, and `SessionResolver::find` drops open
  rollouts whose first line is a sub-agent's
  (`without_codex_subagents`). Tests: tests/bellwether.rs
  `codex_meta_full_reads_id_and_subagent`,
  `codex_candidates_skip_subagent_rollouts`,
  `resolver_finds_codex_root_beside_child`.
- 2026-11-06, src/resolver.rs: open files are matched against the
  resolver's own folders. `log_path_in` (new, with `LogRoots`) takes
  the Claude projects, Codex sessions, Cursor projects and pi folders;
  `log_path` keeps its signature and calls it with
  `LogRoots::in_home(home)`. `find` passes `codex_dir` and
  `projects_dir` (set from `CODEX_HOME` / `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` by the
  caller), then tries the home folders as upstream did. Tests:
  tests/bellwether.rs `log_path_in_uses_codex_home_and_skips_children`,
  `resolver_finds_codex_root_beside_child`; upstream
  `resolver_prefers_open_file_then_codex_cwd_match` still passes.
- 2026-11-06, src/conversation/mod.rs: Codex 0.167 records. `exec` and
  `js` calls are labelled by the `tools.exec_command` /
  `tools.apply_patch` calls in their JavaScript (`codex_call_label`,
  `codex_inner_calls`): a command with its `cmd` as summary (the first,
  plus " (+N more)"), else "Edited files" with the patch's paths, else
  "Ran a script". A plain `apply_patch` call's summary is its paths
  too (`patch_files`, `codex_patch_files`). `spawn_agent` and
  `wait_agent` get their own labels. A `response_item` of type
  `agent_message` becomes a Status item (`codex_agent_status`):
  "<sender> finished: <payload, 200 characters>" or "Sent a task to
  <recipient>". Tests: tests/bellwether.rs
  `codex_exec_command_is_a_command`, `codex_exec_apply_patch_is_an_edit`,
  `codex_spawn_and_wait_labels`, `codex_agent_message_is_a_status`,
  `other_exec_code_is_a_script`.
- 2026-11-06, tests/bellwether.rs (new): the tests above, on the
  scrubbed recordings in tests/fixtures/sessions.
- 2026-11-07, src/conversation/mod.rs: `hc send` from another core
  types `<hc from="<core>/ppid:N">text</hc>`, which `user_visible`
  dropped as tagged text. `hc_sent_text` (new) matches exactly that
  wrapper (the whole message, a `from` of `<core>/ppid:<digits>`, the
  text up to the final `</hc>`, unescaped as hc writes it) and
  `user_visible` judges the inner text as it would typed text. Other
  tagged text is still hidden. Test: tests/bellwether.rs
  `hc_wrapper_keeps_the_senders_text`.
- 2026-11-07, src/model.rs and src/conversation/mod.rs: `ToolCall`
  gains `edited`, the files a Codex `apply_patch` call, or the
  `tools.apply_patch` calls in an `exec` / `js` input, add, update or
  delete, read with `codex_patch_files` from the whole input when the
  call is parsed. `input` is still cut at 4 KB for display, and a
  patch read from it lost the paths past the cut (and, for a quoted
  JavaScript patch, its closing quote, so the path ran on into the
  escaped patch text). Test: tests/bellwether.rs
  `codex_patch_paths_come_from_the_whole_input`.
- 2026-11-07, src/conversation/mod.rs and src/lib.rs: a sub-agent's
  own file parses as a session of its own. `FileScope` (new: `Root`,
  the default and upstream's behaviour; `ClaudeSubagent`;
  `CodexChild { from_ordinal }`), `ConversationParser::with_scope` and
  `parse_lines_in` (new; `parse_lines` is `parse_lines_in` with
  `Root`). `ClaudeSubagent` keeps the `isSidechain` lines that every
  line of `subagents/agent-<id>.jsonl` carries and `feed_at` dropped.
  `CodexChild` skips lines whose top-level `ordinal` is below
  `from_ordinal` (the child's `subagent_history_start_ordinal`), where
  the child rollout repeats the parent's history; lines without an
  `ordinal` are kept. Tests: tests/bellwether.rs
  `claude_subagent_file_parses_on_its_own`,
  `root_scope_still_skips_sidechain_lines`,
  `codex_child_starts_at_its_history_ordinal`,
  `codex_child_without_scope_repeats_the_parent`.
- 2026-11-07, src/approval.rs: `screen_prompt` hashes the tool name,
  the command and the box from its question on, through `id_text`
  (new), which drops every whitespace character and the rule glyphs
  `╌ ─ │`. A narrower or wider pane made Claude redraw the box with
  other line breaks and rules of another length, so the id changed
  and the chat showed a second card. The description and tips above
  the command are left out, since they wrap into lines no filter can
  tell apart; a clipped box hashes every line. Tests:
  crates/bw/tests/matchers.rs `rewrap_claude_approval_keeps_its_id`,
  `rewrap_other_command_changes_the_id`; upstream tests in
  src/approval/tests.rs still pass.
